# SEO title and meta description length

Resolved `<title>` and meta description must fit typical SERP limits. Do not ship a short card blurb as the meta description.

| Field | Target | Hard limits |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Title (`metaTitle`, else `title`) | 50–60 characters | 30–60 |
| Meta description | 140–155 characters | 120–160 |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — title truncates in Google (~73 characters)
title: "Best Pillow for Neck Pain: Pillow Cube vs. Talalay Latex vs. Layla Kapok"

// ✅ GOOD — keep the long H1 in `title`, put the SERP title in `metaTitle`
title: "Best Pillow for Neck Pain: Pillow Cube vs. Talalay Latex vs. Layla Kapok"
metaTitle: "Best Pillow for Neck Pain: Cube vs Latex vs Kapok"

// ❌ BAD — product `shortDescription` used as meta (too short)
shortDescription: 'A 20" x 54" shredded memory foam body pillow with a Kool-Flow bamboo-blend cover at a budget price.'

// ✅ GOOD — dedicated metaDescription in range
metaDescription:
  'A 20" x 54" shredded memory foam body pillow with a Kool-Flow bamboo-blend cover at a budget price. Side-sleeper fit, fill, and what you get for the money.'
```

Count the **resolved** strings after fallbacks (`metaTitle ?? title`, `metaDescription ?? shortDescription`). Site-name suffixes are not added on Side Sleeper product/review pages (`title.absolute`). Do not append `| Site` inside `metaTitle` on sites that already use a title template.
